cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Weather Rescue Brazil: nineteenth-century Brazilian weather observations transcribed by a small offline model"
message: "If you use this dataset or the method, please cite it. Attribution is not required by the licence (the transcriptions are CC0); this file is here because citation is how the work becomes findable."
type: dataset
authors:
  - alias: akagabi
    website: "https://github.com/akagabi"
repository-code: "https://github.com/akagabi/weather-rescue-brazil"
url: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/akagabi/weather-rescue-brazil"
abstract: >-
  Daily and dekadal meteorological observations from eleven Brazilian stations
  and one ship, 1882-1890, transcribed from the printed tables of the Annales de
  l'Observatoire Imperial de Rio de Janeiro (French) and the Revista do
  Observatorio (Portuguese). Variables include barometric pressure read seven
  times daily, temperature maxima, minima and means, relative humidity, vapour
  tension, cloudiness, wind direction and force, rainfall, evaporation, ozone and
  actinometry. Transcription is by a Qwen3.5-2B model with a LoRA adapter running
  offline on a laptop; each printed layout is described by a JSON profile
  declaring its columns, units, physical ranges and the arithmetic the page
  asserts about itself, which is used to judge every row without a human.
  No row has been verified line-by-line by a human; the 3,822-cell evaluation
  gold set has been, and is separate from the dataset.
keywords:
  - data rescue
  - historical climatology
  - Brazil
  - nineteenth century
  - table recognition
  - document understanding
license: CC0-1.0
